				"_note": "Statutory-deadline archetype: a filing's whole purpose is 'was it filed on time and is proof retained'. loonaangifte-filing-lifecycle (2026-07-12) gave NL filings a real create->review->confirm->send workflow, so the page now leads with a compact status/tijdvakcode/deadline/response widget (fi-status) before the full filing data widget, and exposes the klaarzetten/bevestigen/verzenden/heropenen/corrigeren transitions via lifecycleActions (Timesheet pattern). No stats-block KPI tile is used for Status/Deadline: the vendored app-manifest-v2 schema's stat/stats-block `metric` only supports count/sum aggregation, which cannot echo a non-numeric field (enum/date) of the current object, so fi-status is a `data` widget instead -- schema-valid and functionally equivalent (prominent, top-of-page). No related panel (the schema carries no employeeId/administrationId or any other object-FK -- a filing is an organisation-level record, not scoped to a person). Files is included full-width for the filed submission/deposit proof, justified by the schema's own retainedUntil/furnishedToRecipientDate/filedWithAuthorityDate retention-evidence fields (NL 7yr / DE 6yr / US 4yr retention obligations). No calendar/comms leaves -- deadline is a plain date field, not an appointment/event linkedType. Audit history is a sidebar tab.",
